# tests/xfail.list -- expected failures.
#
# One test file basename per line, e.g.
#
#     test_kernel_cache.sh
#
# Blank lines and `#` comments (whole-line or trailing) are ignored.
#
# Semantics enforced by tests/run.sh:
#   * A listed test that FAILS is reported XFAIL and counts as a pass.
#   * A listed test that PASSES is reported XPASS and fails the whole run.
#
# The XPASS rule is deliberate: it forces whoever fixes the underlying bug to
# delete the entry here, so this list can never silently rot into a list of
# tests that are no longer broken.
#
# This file is intentionally empty: there are no known failures today.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# test_hooks_apply.sh -- the two pre-6.17 hooks do not apply cleanly to the
# pinned old tree (linux-6.12.112).  They still apply (exit 0, no .rej), but
# patch reports an offset, which means the hook's context no longer lines up
# with the kernel source it patches:
#
#   patch_patch_cs8409.c.diff   offset 170 lines (hunks 1-3)
#   patch_patch_cs8409.h.diff   offset 3 lines   (hunks 2-4)
#
# The pre-6.17 installer's implemented range tops out at 5.19 (see
# install.cirrus.driver.pre617.sh:233-237), so 6.12 is already past what it
# claims to support and the installer prints "Kernel version later than
# implemented version - there may be build problems" for it.  The offsets are
# therefore expected, but they are still drift: the hooks are pinned to an
# older kernel_sources/ snapshot.
#
# Fixing the hooks is a separate story.  Until then this test fails on purpose
# so the drift stays visible instead of being papered over.
test_hooks_apply.sh

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# test_installer_exit_status.sh -- HDA-05.  The installers report success after
# a failed install: dkms.sh ends with `popd > /dev/null` (line 44), and both
# installers end their dkms branches with `ls -lA $update_dir` followed by a
# bare `exit` (install.cirrus.driver.sh:73-74, pre617:77-78).  The download
# path has the same shape: `[[ $? -ne 0 ]] && echo ... && exit`
# (install.cirrus.driver.sh:203, pre617:219) exits 0 because the echo succeeds.
#
# Which cases really fail today (measured on macOS, non-root):
#   FAIL  dkms.sh, `dkms install` failed                       -> exits 0
#   FAIL  install.cirrus.driver.sh -i, `dkms install` failed   -> exits 0
#   FAIL  install.cirrus.driver.pre617.sh -i, `dkms install` failed -> exits 0
#   FAIL  install.cirrus.driver.sh -r, `dkms remove` failed    -> exits 0
#   FAIL  install.cirrus.driver.pre617.sh -r, `dkms remove` failed  -> exits 0
#
# The remaining cases -- the non-dkms path of both installers, with `make
# install`, `wget` or `tar` failing -- cannot be driven on this machine at all
# and print BLOCKED instead of passing or failing.  The installer's
# kernel-headers probe (`[ -d /usr/src/linux-headers-<ver> ]`,
# install.cirrus.driver.sh:97-128, pre617:114-145) is a bash builtin on an
# absolute path, so no PATH shim can influence it, and /usr/src is not
# writable here; the probe exits 1 before the code under test.  They are
# written out and will run on a Linux box with kernel headers installed.  No
# test seam was added to production for this story.
#
# The positive controls live in tests/test_installer_exit_status_controls.sh,
# which is NOT listed here and must stay green.
#
# remove when B1 (HDA-10) lands
test_installer_exit_status.sh
